// Vitest Snapshot v1, https://vitest.dev/guide/snapshot.html

exports[`R3.10 RngExplainer > R3.10 the explainer's content matches its snapshot: what earns Best, how the roll works, why practise mixing (ADR 0024) 1`] = `
<div
  class="flex flex-col gap-4 text-sm"
  data-testid="rng-explainer-content"
>
  <section
    class="flex flex-col gap-2"
  >
    <h3
      class="font-semibold"
    >
      What earns Best
    </h3>
    <p>
      Best is always the action with the highest EV (expected value). Any other action whose EV loss is within the noise floor is graded Correct. The roll never changes your grade.
    </p>
  </section>
  <section
    class="flex flex-col gap-2"
  >
    <h3
      class="font-semibold"
    >
      How the roll works
    </h3>
    <p>
      Before you act, the app rolls a number from 1 to 100 and shows it on a scale, with nothing else. Weigh how often the strategy takes each of your options, then choose the one the roll points to.
    </p>
    <div
      class="flex flex-col gap-1"
      data-revealed="false"
      data-testid="rng-roller"
    >
      <div
        class="flex items-center justify-between gap-2"
      >
        <p
          aria-live="polite"
          class="text-sm font-medium"
        >
          Mixed-frequency mode
        </p>
      </div>
      <div
        class="relative h-5"
      >
        <span
          class="absolute top-0 -translate-x-1/2 whitespace-nowrap text-xs font-semibold tabular-nums"
          data-testid="rng-roll-label"
          style="left: 36.5%;"
        >
          Roll 37
        </span>
      </div>
      <div
        aria-label="Roll 37 on a scale from 1 to 100"
        class="relative"
        role="img"
      >
        <div
          class="h-12 w-full rounded border border-border bg-surface-sunken"
        />
        <span
          aria-hidden="true"
          class="absolute -top-1 -bottom-1 w-0.5 -translate-x-1/2 bg-text"
          data-testid="rng-marker"
          style="left: 36.5%;"
        />
      </div>
      <div
        aria-hidden="true"
        class="relative h-4 text-xs text-muted"
      >
        <span
          class="absolute top-0 -translate-x-1/2 tabular-nums"
          data-testid="rng-tick"
          style="left: 0.5%;"
        >
          1
        </span>
        <span
          class="absolute top-0 -translate-x-1/2 tabular-nums"
          data-testid="rng-tick"
          style="left: 24.5%;"
        >
          25
        </span>
        <span
          class="absolute top-0 -translate-x-1/2 tabular-nums"
          data-testid="rng-tick"
          style="left: 49.5%;"
        >
          50
        </span>
        <span
          class="absolute top-0 -translate-x-1/2 tabular-nums"
          data-testid="rng-tick"
          style="left: 74.5%;"
        >
          75
        </span>
        <span
          class="absolute top-0 -translate-x-1/2 tabular-nums"
          data-testid="rng-tick"
          style="left: 99.5%;"
        >
          100
        </span>
      </div>
    </div>
    <p>
      After your decision the same scale shows the bands. Your hand's actions are lined up from passive to aggressive: fold, then check or call, then bets and raises from small to large, each as wide as its frequency. Example: 40 percent call and 60 percent raise means rolls 1 to 40 call and 41 to 100 raise, so roll 37 lands in the call band.
    </p>
    <div
      class="flex flex-col gap-1"
      data-revealed="true"
      data-selected-index="0"
      data-testid="rng-roller"
    >
      <div
        class="flex items-center justify-between gap-2"
      >
        <p
          aria-live="polite"
          class="text-sm font-medium"
        >
          Roll 37 fell on Call
        </p>
      </div>
      <div
        class="relative h-5"
      >
        <span
          class="absolute top-0 -translate-x-1/2 whitespace-nowrap text-xs font-semibold tabular-nums"
          data-testid="rng-roll-label"
          style="left: 36.5%;"
        >
          Roll 37
        </span>
      </div>
      <div
        class="relative"
      >
        <ol
          aria-label="Mixed-frequency bands"
          class="flex h-12 w-full overflow-hidden rounded border border-border motion-safe:transition-[clip-path] motion-safe:duration-500 motion-safe:ease-out motion-reduce:transition-none"
          data-reveal="pending"
          style="clip-path: inset(0px 100% 0px 0px);"
        >
          <li
            aria-current="true"
            class="flex min-w-0 items-center justify-center gap-1 overflow-hidden border-r border-black/20 px-1 text-xs text-slate-900 bg-(--action-light) dark:bg-(--action-dark) outline outline-2 -outline-offset-2 outline-focus"
            data-action-index="0"
            data-range="1-40"
            style="--action-light: #4ade80; --action-dark: #22c55e; background-image: radial-gradient(rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.35) 1px, transparent 1.5px); background-size: 5px 5px; width: 40%;"
            title="1-40 Call"
          >
            <span
              class="flex items-center gap-1 truncate rounded bg-white/80 px-1"
            >
              <span
                class="inline-flex items-center gap-1"
              >
                <span
                  aria-hidden="true"
                  class="inline-block h-3.5 w-3.5 shrink-0 rounded-sm border border-black/20 bg-(--action-light) dark:bg-(--action-dark)"
                  data-pattern="dots"
                  data-testid="action-swatch"
                  style="--action-light: #4ade80; --action-dark: #22c55e; background-image: radial-gradient(rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.35) 1px, transparent 1.5px); background-size: 5px 5px;"
                />
                <span
                  aria-hidden="true"
                  class="font-mono text-xs font-bold"
                >
                  C
                </span>
              </span>
              <span
                data-testid="rng-band-label"
              >
                1-40 Call
              </span>
            </span>
          </li>
          <li
            class="flex min-w-0 items-center justify-center gap-1 overflow-hidden border-r border-black/20 px-1 text-xs text-slate-900 bg-(--action-light) dark:bg-(--action-dark)"
            data-action-index="1"
            data-range="41-100"
            style="--action-light: #f87171; --action-dark: #ef4444; background-image: repeating-linear-gradient(45deg, rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.35) 0 2px, transparent 2px 6px); width: 60%;"
            title="41-100 Raise to 2.5bb"
          >
            <span
              class="flex items-center gap-1 truncate rounded bg-white/80 px-1"
            >
              <span
                class="inline-flex items-center gap-1"
              >
                <span
                  aria-hidden="true"
                  class="inline-block h-3.5 w-3.5 shrink-0 rounded-sm border border-black/20 bg-(--action-light) dark:bg-(--action-dark)"
                  data-pattern="diagonal"
                  data-testid="action-swatch"
                  style="--action-light: #f87171; --action-dark: #ef4444; background-image: repeating-linear-gradient(45deg, rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.35) 0 2px, transparent 2px 6px);"
                />
                <span
                  aria-hidden="true"
                  class="font-mono text-xs font-bold"
                >
                  R
                </span>
              </span>
              <span
                data-testid="rng-band-label"
              >
                41-100 Raise to 2.5bb
              </span>
            </span>
          </li>
        </ol>
        <span
          aria-hidden="true"
          class="absolute -top-1 -bottom-1 w-0.5 -translate-x-1/2 bg-text"
          data-testid="rng-marker"
          style="left: 36.5%;"
        />
      </div>
      <ul
        aria-label="Mixed-frequency band legend"
        class="flex flex-wrap gap-x-4 gap-y-1 text-xs text-muted"
      >
        <li
          class="flex items-center gap-1"
        >
          <span
            class="inline-flex items-center gap-1"
          >
            <span
              aria-hidden="true"
              class="inline-block h-3.5 w-3.5 shrink-0 rounded-sm border border-black/20 bg-(--action-light) dark:bg-(--action-dark)"
              data-pattern="dots"
              data-testid="action-swatch"
              style="--action-light: #4ade80; --action-dark: #22c55e; background-image: radial-gradient(rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.35) 1px, transparent 1.5px); background-size: 5px 5px;"
            />
            <span
              aria-hidden="true"
              class="font-mono text-xs font-bold"
            >
              C
            </span>
          </span>
          <span>
            1-40 Call
          </span>
        </li>
        <li
          class="flex items-center gap-1"
        >
          <span
            class="inline-flex items-center gap-1"
          >
            <span
              aria-hidden="true"
              class="inline-block h-3.5 w-3.5 shrink-0 rounded-sm border border-black/20 bg-(--action-light) dark:bg-(--action-dark)"
              data-pattern="diagonal"
              data-testid="action-swatch"
              style="--action-light: #f87171; --action-dark: #ef4444; background-image: repeating-linear-gradient(45deg, rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.35) 0 2px, transparent 2px 6px);"
            />
            <span
              aria-hidden="true"
              class="font-mono text-xs font-bold"
            >
              R
            </span>
          </span>
          <span>
            41-100 Raise to 2.5bb
          </span>
        </li>
      </ul>
    </div>
    <p
      class="text-muted"
    >
      A separate mark then says whether you followed the roll. It shows how well you mix; it is not part of the grade.
    </p>
  </section>
  <section
    class="flex flex-col gap-2"
  >
    <h3
      class="font-semibold"
    >
      Why practise mixing
    </h3>
    <p>
      Some hands play more than one action, calling some of the time and raising the rest. Such a hand is close to indifferent between those actions, and the mix protects your range: if you always played it the same way, an observant opponent could learn which hands take which line. Mixed-frequency mode trains you to take each action about as often as the strategy does.
    </p>
  </section>
</div>
`;
